# Title: Deletion of Volume Shadow Copies via WMI with PowerShell
# ID: 21ff4ca9-f13a-41ad-b828-0077b2af2e40
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
# Date: 2022-09-20
# Tags: attack.impact, attack.t1490
# Description: Detects deletion of Windows Volume Shadow Copies with PowerShell code and Get-WMIObject. This technique is used by numerous ransomware families such as Sodinokibi/REvil
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*.Delete()*" OR process_exec="*Remove-WmiObject*" OR process_exec="*rwmi*" OR process_exec="*Remove-CimInstance*" OR process_exec="*rcim*")) AND ((process_exec="*Get-WmiObject*" OR process_exec="*gwmi*" OR process_exec="*Get-CimInstance*" OR process_exec="*gcim*")) AND (process_exec="*Win32_ShadowCopy*"))
